    {
      "id": "page-template-instructions",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Page Template Sketch",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -2060,
        "y": 260
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "guided-by",
          "key": "guided-by",
          "label": "guided by",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180,
          "role": "relationship",
          "allowedEdgeTypes": [
            "reference"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "page-template"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Page template (sketch)\n\nA graph template, `templates/page`. Names and fields are illustrative.\n\n## The page\n\n- The Declaration exposes the page as its full-page view. The summary and icon views are derived from the same pieces.\n- The page is a flow of ordered pieces. Order starts as graph order.\n\n## Piece roles (a starting catalog)\n\n| Role | Job | Typical fields |\n|---|---|---|\n| Masthead | Says whose page this is | eyebrow, title, subtitle |\n| Hero | The one thing to understand first | headline, body, call to action |\n| Section | A titled block of content | title, body |\n| Callout | Something that must not be missed | tone, body |\n| Route list | Where to go next | routes, each with a destination and a prominence |\n| Media | An image, diagram or embed | source, caption |\n| Aside | Secondary or related material | title, body |\n| Footer | Utilities and provenance | links, notes |\n\nPieces that lead somewhere are portals, so navigation stays graph-native.\n\n## It keeps itself current\n\n- One Handler for any piece changed and one for the graph structure changing, each calling one Method that re-assembles the page view and writes it into the exposed views.\n- The Method declares those views as its only effects.\n\n## Not in scope\n\nRegions, breakpoints, themes and animation. Layout and styling belong to the document view that already exists."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        }
      },
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "guided-by",
          "key": "guided-by",
          "label": "guided by",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
