        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "A Page Is a Graph of Pieces",
        "statement": "The Page Template exists to create regions on the page background, so the content of a graph can be sorted visually into logical places. Each region is a page piece with a role (masthead, hero, section, callout, route list, media, aside, footer), its own class, its own content, and its own view. The template builds the page's document from the pieces' views and returns them stacked in one view node, which the consumer page renders. An author edits one region, an agent can add or reorder regions, and a region can serve more than one page.",
        "status": "framed",
        "confidence": "unproven",
        "notes": "Started from scratch. The Public Arrival Template (github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/public-arrival-template/root.node) is one input among many: the Page Parts Inventory below reads twenty graphs and is the evidence for which pieces a page needs. The front door idea (github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/twilite-front-door/root.node) is the first page this should be able to build.",
        "definitionKey": "idea",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/idea-template/classes/nodes/idea.node-class.node",
