            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Inventory of page parts",
        "findings": "Twenty graphs were read: nine templates (Public Arrival, Wikipedia Article, Question-Driven Explanation, Collection, Workboard, Topic, Plan, Brainstorm, Idea) and eleven pages. Nine of the eleven pages have real parts; two (Twilite and Products) are stubs with only a title and a type definition. Every one of the nine has a masthead, and seven of the nine have places to go, as routes or as connected portals. Regions that hold graph content appear twice by hand: the gallery (three headings with twelve connected portals) and the workboard (five lanes). Three different mechanisms express order or containment: graph order, edge classes (arrival.contains, arrival.offers-route), and ordinal edge labels on the workboard. Media appears only as icons. Some parts fit no role: Legend, manifest and type definition are infrastructure, the domain classes (question, topic, plan, idea and so on) are content that a page would sort into regions rather than page roles, and the Wikipedia article source is an article-shaped piece with its own structure. The full table is in the Page Parts Inventory note.",
        "sourceUrl": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/page-template/root.node",
        "sourceType": "other",
        "definitionKey": "idea-research",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea-research",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/idea-template/classes/nodes/idea-research.node-class.node",
