    {
      "id": "page-template-inventory",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Page Parts Inventory",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -2060,
        "y": 1160
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "guided-by",
          "key": "guided-by",
          "label": "guided by",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180,
          "role": "relationship",
          "allowedEdgeTypes": [
            "reference"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "page-template"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Page Parts Inventory\n\nTwenty graphs read for the parts a page is made of. Templates first, then pages.\n\n## Templates\n\n| Graph | Parts |\n|---|---|\n| Public Arrival | arrival (eyebrow, title, body); three arrival-routes (destination, prominence, kind); an arrival-section (Utilities); two arrival-utilities (Docs, GitHub); a landing note |\n| Wikipedia Article | one article source (title, lead, sections, attribution); six content notes; two portals |\n| Question-Driven Explanation | topic, question, answer, source, example, caveat, summary |\n| Collection | a window controller script, a landing note, a membership note, one portal |\n| Workboard | a workboard node; five lanes (Inbox, Now, Next, Waiting, Recently Completed) with empty-state notes; one portal |\n| Topic | topic, concept, claim, mechanism, perspective, source, synthesis |\n| Plan | plan, goal, phase, action, milestone, decision, constraint, risk, contingency |\n| Brainstorm | idea, question, decision, constraint, reference note |\n| Idea | idea, problem, audience, approach, question, assumption, research, evidence, alternative, risk, next step |\n\n## Pages\n\n| Graph | Parts |\n|---|---|\n| Twilite Zone (public root) | arrival masthead; two routes; an Explore section with three utilities; an explanatory note |\n| Getting Started | arrival masthead and four routes |\n| Gallery | a masthead note and three regions (Living Collections, Featured Graphs, Build Something) holding twelve connected portals |\n| Tutorial | a lesson hero; five concepts; an example with a call to action; a challenge; a checkpoint; nine portals including a way back to the public root |\n| Twilite LLC | a masthead note; Mission, What We Are Building, Operating Principles and Current Stage sections; four portals |\n| The Boulevard | a title and a landing note, with summary and icon views |\n| Documentation | a root note and twelve sections (Onboarding, Contracts Index, Validation, Data vs UI Boundary, Graph Primitives and others) |\n| Public Atelier (Michael's root) | a title; three sections (Civic Face, Signals, Invitation); a document summary; a contact note; twenty-two portals |\n| Michael's Workboard | five lanes with fourteen portals, sequenced by ordinal edge labels |\n| Twilite, Products | stubs: a title and a type definition, no page parts |\n\n## Roles that recur\n\n| Role | Where it appears | Example classes today |\n|---|---|---|\n| Masthead | 9 of 9 pages with parts | arrival, title, tutorial-title, a level-one heading |\n| Route list | 7 of 9 | arrival-route, portals with a prominence |\n| Section | 5 | arrival-section, section, tutorial-concept, a level-two heading |\n| Region holding content | 2 | the gallery's and workboard's headings with connected items |\n| Secondary or utility list | 1 page, plus the Arrival template | arrival-utility |\n| Summary | 1 page, plus the explanation and topic templates | document-summary, qa-summary, topic-synthesis |\n| Callout | 2 | tutorial-challenge, tutorial-checkpoint, a contact note |\n| Footer or way back | 2 | a \"Back to Public Root\" portal |\n| Media | 0 | none beyond icons |\n\n## How order and membership are expressed today\n\n- **Graph order** for plain nodes and stroke paint order.\n- **Edge classes** in the arrival classes: `arrival.contains` and `arrival.offers-route`.\n- **Ordinal edge labels** on the workboard: `now · 1`, `then · 3`.\n- **Labeled relationships** in the gallery: `exhibits`, `features`, `opens`.\n\n## What did not fit\n\n- Infrastructure: Legend, manifest, type definition.\n- Domain content (question, topic, plan, idea and similar classes). These are what a page sorts into regions, not page roles.\n- The Wikipedia article source, which is an article-shaped piece with its own structure."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        }
      },
      "handles": [
